WEBVTT

00:00:01.566 --> 00:00:05.499
-[Narrator] Welcome to Module 1 Accessibility Overview.

00:00:07.666 --> 00:00:10.999
Imagine opening a new online course.

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:12.766
There are no captions.

00:00:12.766 --> 00:00:15.066
The text is hard to read.

00:00:15.066 --> 00:00:17.366
Buttons don't tell you what they do.

00:00:17.366 --> 00:00:19.466
You try to make it work,

00:00:19.466 --> 00:00:21.666
but the message is already clear;

00:00:21.666 --> 00:00:25.366
this space was not designed with you in mind.

00:00:25.366 --> 00:00:27.532
That is the power of design.

00:00:27.533 --> 00:00:29.599
It communicates instantly.

00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:31.233
And in learning spaces,

00:00:31.233 --> 00:00:33.699
that message should always be:

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:35.466
You belong here.

00:00:35.466 --> 00:00:38.732
Accessibility isn't something we add at the end.

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:42.166
It starts at the very beginning, 

00:00:42.166 --> 00:00:46.199
when we choose fonts, write alternative text,

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:48.466
and set up captions.

00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:52.800
Accessibility is more than a checklist.

00:00:53.133 --> 00:00:54.466
It's a mindset;

00:00:54.466 --> 00:00:56.999
a commitment that no learner should be left out

00:00:57.000 --> 00:00:59.533
because of how a course is built.

00:00:59.833 --> 00:01:02.599
That's where WCAG, 

00:01:02.600 --> 00:01:06.533
the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines, comes in.

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:12.000
WCAG turns the idea of access for all

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:13.633
into practical steps.

00:01:14.300 --> 00:01:17.533
How we caption our videos, structure text,

00:01:17.533 --> 00:01:20.466
choose contrast, and design for screen readers

00:01:20.466 --> 00:01:21.532
and keyboards.

00:01:22.133 --> 00:01:25.033
The Web Content Accessibility Guidelines

00:01:25.033 --> 00:01:29.033
has organized their guidelines under four principles

00:01:29.033 --> 00:01:30.599
commonly known as:

00:01:30.600 --> 00:01:36.166
Perceivable, Operable, Understandable, and Robust.

00:01:36.166 --> 00:01:39.266
Following these guidelines ensures that digital materials

00:01:39.266 --> 00:01:43.432
are inclusive and consumable for all users.

00:01:45.033 --> 00:01:47.066
When we design our courses this way,

00:01:47.066 --> 00:01:49.866
it doesn't just help learners with disabilities, 

00:01:49.866 --> 00:01:52.432
it helps second language learners,

00:01:52.433 --> 00:01:55.733
someone learning on a phone, and simply put,

00:01:55.733 --> 00:01:59.133
it makes our courses better for everyone.

00:02:01.366 --> 00:02:04.066
Accessible design isn't just required.

00:02:04.066 --> 00:02:05.399
It's responsible.

00:02:05.400 --> 00:02:07.133
It's human.

00:02:07.133 --> 00:02:10.399
As you move through this course, start with one intention;

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:13.866
design so that everyone belongs.

00:02:14.366 --> 00:02:18.099
Perceivable design; making content reachable

00:02:18.100 --> 00:02:19.966
for every learner.

00:02:19.966 --> 00:02:22.699
Perceivable design matters because

00:02:22.700 --> 00:02:26.233
not everyone experiences content in the same way.

00:02:26.233 --> 00:02:29.533
Some learners see, some listen.

00:02:29.533 --> 00:02:32.366
Others rely on assistive technologies,

00:02:32.366 --> 00:02:35.932
like screen readers or voice recognition tools.

00:02:35.933 --> 00:02:39.599
If your course only works in one format,

00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:44.466
such as slides with only visuals or audio without captions,

00:02:44.466 --> 00:02:47.632
you unintentionally place some learners

00:02:47.633 --> 00:02:51.033
outside the learning experience.

00:02:51.033 --> 00:02:53.133
To create perceivable content,

00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:56.766
we need to present information in multiple ways

00:02:56.766 --> 00:02:58.999
so all learners can access it.

00:03:00.466 --> 00:03:02.366
As you design your course,

00:03:02.366 --> 00:03:05.366
keep these questions in mind.

00:03:05.366 --> 00:03:10.199
If someone can't see it, can they hear or read it?

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:12.033
If someone can't hear it,

00:03:12.033 --> 00:03:14.666
can they see or read it?

00:03:14.666 --> 00:03:16.866
If someone can't stream it,

00:03:16.866 --> 00:03:20.599
do they have another way to access it?

00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:22.833
That's perceivable design, 

00:03:22.833 --> 00:03:25.799
ensuring that essential information is available

00:03:25.800 --> 00:03:29.500
to every learner, regardless of how they access it.

00:03:31.566 --> 00:03:34.499
Operable design: making content usable

00:03:34.500 --> 00:03:36.233
for every learner.

00:03:37.433 --> 00:03:40.966
Operability means learners should be able to navigate

00:03:40.966 --> 00:03:44.832
and use a course without guessing or struggling,

00:03:44.833 --> 00:03:47.366
regardless of whether they use a mouse,

00:03:47.366 --> 00:03:50.166
keyboard, or assistive technology.

00:03:50.166 --> 00:03:53.799
Keyboard navigation is a key part of this.

00:03:53.800 --> 00:03:59.433
Links, buttons, forms, and media controls

00:03:59.433 --> 00:04:02.299
must be accessible through the Tab key

00:04:02.300 --> 00:04:06.066
in a clear logical order with a visible focus,

00:04:06.066 --> 00:04:09.532
so learners know where they are on the screen.

00:04:09.533 --> 00:04:12.766
Controls also need meaningful labels

00:04:12.766 --> 00:04:15.599
that describe their function, like

00:04:15.600 --> 00:04:19.966
"Submit Assignment" or "Play Video,"

00:04:19.966 --> 00:04:24.099
instead of vague terms, like "Click Here."

00:04:25.266 --> 00:04:26.932
Designing for operability

00:04:26.933 --> 00:04:29.466
doesn't require reinventing your course.

00:04:29.766 --> 00:04:32.366
It means making existing tools

00:04:32.366 --> 00:04:36.099
usable across different input methods.

00:04:36.700 --> 00:04:39.133
When we design with these in mind,

00:04:39.133 --> 00:04:40.666
we remove barriers and

00:04:40.666 --> 00:04:42.932
welcome more learners from the start.

00:04:43.433 --> 00:04:45.266
Keep these questions in mind

00:04:45.266 --> 00:04:48.832
as you are including directives in your course.

00:04:49.833 --> 00:04:51.933
If someone can't use a mouse,

00:04:51.933 --> 00:04:55.199
can they still complete the activity?

00:04:55.200 --> 00:04:57.600
If someone can't see the screen,

00:04:57.600 --> 00:05:00.033
can they still submit the form?

00:05:02.933 --> 00:05:05.533
Understandable design: making content

00:05:05.533 --> 00:05:08.166
easy to follow for every learner.

00:05:08.700 --> 00:05:11.600
Not all barriers to learning are technical.

00:05:11.600 --> 00:05:15.900
Sometimes the course functions, but it is confusing,

00:05:15.900 --> 00:05:19.233
unpredictable or hard to follow.

00:05:19.233 --> 00:05:21.699
Understandable design means

00:05:21.700 --> 00:05:23.233
creating course content

00:05:23.233 --> 00:05:28.599
that is clear, straightforward, and easy to follow.

00:05:28.600 --> 00:05:31.400
So learners always know what to do,

00:05:31.400 --> 00:05:34.233
where to go, and what to expect.

00:05:34.966 --> 00:05:39.632
Instructions should be plain, specific, and actionable.

00:05:40.166 --> 00:05:42.099
While layouts should follow a

00:05:42.100 --> 00:05:46.300
clear visual structure and consistent navigation.

00:05:46.300 --> 00:05:50.700
When clarity, consistency, and guidance are built in,

00:05:50.700 --> 00:05:53.266
learners can focus on learning,

00:05:53.266 --> 00:05:55.799
not figuring out the course.

00:05:57.066 --> 00:06:00.532
Robust content is about making sure your

00:06:00.533 --> 00:06:04.599
course works smoothly on any device, browser,

00:06:04.600 --> 00:06:06.700
or operating system.

00:06:06.700 --> 00:06:11.766
This principle is essential for web-based content,

00:06:11.766 --> 00:06:14.832
but it has less direct relevance

00:06:14.833 --> 00:06:17.933
for standard Word documents.

00:06:17.933 --> 00:06:24.499
Examples include videos, links, quizzes, downloads,

00:06:24.500 --> 00:06:26.200
or interactive activities.

00:06:28.666 --> 00:06:31.799
In the following modules, you will learn to create documents

00:06:31.800 --> 00:06:33.566
that are reflective of

00:06:33.566 --> 00:06:38.432
perceivable, operable, and understandable principles,

00:06:38.433 --> 00:06:40.866
adhering to accessibility guidelines

00:06:40.866 --> 00:06:43.999
and providing more suitable experiences

00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:45.466
for your students.

00:06:46.700 --> 00:06:52.300
In digital learning, that is not just a best practice, 

00:06:52.300 --> 00:06:54.366
it's our responsibility.
